.TH _PRINTF 3 "22 July 2025" "Custom Version" "Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
_printf \- our version of printf (handles %c, %s, %%, %d, %i)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"
.br
.B int _printf(const char *format, ...);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B _printf()
is a simplified implementation of the standard printf function. It displays data to the standard output using a format string.
Supported format specifiers include:
.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.
.TP
.B %s
Prints a string of characters.
.TP
.B %d, %i
Prints a decimal integer.
.TP
.B %%
Prints a literal percent sign.
If an invalid format specifier is encountered, both the `%` and the following character are printed as-is.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the total number of characters printed to the output (excluded the null bytes).
If  it is an error the return will be negative.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
_printf("Hello %s! You scored %d%% on the test.\\n", "Alice", 95);
.fi
Output:
.in
Hello Alice! You scored 95% on the test.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR printf(3)
